module gunbc.plans.host_effect_orchestration

import gunbc.plan { Plan, DissolutionTrigger, HasTrigger }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, TableBlock, AlignNone, CodeBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, cell, row }

fn host_effect_orchestration_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Status:** design note for sign-off. Co-authored smart-newt-512 (dag-managed-infra) + neat-boar-71 (BMC onboarding). **Neither lane mints the interface until the shape is signed** (operator + bright-stag-194). Until then host effects ride neat-boar's `host_exec()` placeholder seam — *using* it, not minting the interface; every call migrates onto `apply()` in one move once signed."),
    h2(text: "0. Aim (operator, 2026-06-24)"),
    p(text: "Manage the **whole server lifecycle on `.dag`** — install / manage / decom — coherent and tested-working, moving **off pure shell transport onto real `.dag` orchestration**. Two standing constraints:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Minimal central dependencies.** Move toward the simplest representation: the host **bootstraps itself as far as it can** (via BMC or otherwise) — fewer things to manage, no central orchestrator holding SSH keys to every host (the star-topology cost). The end-state is *pull*, not *push*."),
      li(text: "**No ctrl split.** The JS control plane shrinks to zero. Honest metric = **ctrl LOC deleted per responsibility moved**, not lines added anywhere (§7 seed-shrink applied to the control plane)."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. The shape (the one thing to sign off)"),
    p(text: "Both lanes independently converged on this: today's \"emit a shell artifact + external runner\" and \"gunbc-run dispatches `shell.Exec.Run` over SSH\" are **not two regimes** — they are realizations of **one interface**, varying along **two orthogonal axes** (DESIGN §3b transport, §3c policy):"),
    CodeBlock {
      code: "apply(target: NodeControlPlane, effect: HostEffect, policy: Policy) -> Receipt   # fail-closed, typed, located\n\n   NodeControlPlane = HostOs(node)        # in-band  — transport ∈ \{SshShell, LocalShell, SystemdUnit, EmitArtifactThenThinRun\}\n                    | BmcController(node)  # out-of-band — transport ∈ \{RedfishRest\}\n   HostEffect       = ShellCommand\{script\} | RedfishAction\{resource, verb, body\} | …   # COPRODUCT of effect-kinds\n   Policy (§3c)     = OneShotIdempotent | ConvergeToFixpoint\n   Receipt          = located/typed core + poll-until-converged task state (NOT just exit-0)"
    },
    p(text: "**One interface × N control-planes × N transports × N effect-kinds × N policies.** Dispatch (selecting transport+policy for a (control-plane, effect-kind)) is *itself* realization → it sits peripheral; only the agnostic effect shape + `apply()` stay central (DESIGN §3 \"the dispatch that selects a realization is itself realization\")."),
    p(text: "Three refinements proved by driving srv3's BMC live (neat-boar-71), each load-bearing:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Target-duality.** A logical node has *two* control planes — in-band host OS (ssh/systemd) and out-of-band BMC (Redfish) — so `apply` targets a **control plane**, not a host address. Pre-OS lifecycle phases (`FactoryDefault → OsInstalled`) are reachable **out-of-band ONLY**: the OS doesn't exist yet, only the BMC does. Both resolve over `fleet_intent` (which already binds `HostIdentity` + `BmcEndpoint` per node)."),
      li(text: "**`HostEffect` is a coproduct, not a shell string.** A Redfish op is `BootSourceOverride\{target:Pxe, enabled:Once\}` then `Reset\{ForceRestart\}` — typed actions, not bash. A stringly `command` field would be the §3 anemic leaf; ssh's shell-string is *one arm*. Dispatch on (control-plane × transport × effect-kind) makes an **incompatible combination (e.g. `RedfishAction` over `SshShell`) a typed mismatch, unwritable by construction** (§5) — not a silent failure."),
      li(text: "**Async/polled Receipt.** Redfish `Reset` returns before the machine reboots; the real outcome is observed by **polling** (BootSourceOverrideEnabled flips `Once → Disabled` when firmware consumes it). So the Receipt carries poll-until-converged task state. This *reinforces* the policy axis: BMC ops are **intrinsically converge-shaped** even in a \"one-shot\" call — `ConvergeToFixpoint` is a property of the effect, not just of ssh-vs-drift."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Layer split** (keeps the import arrow pointing toward std; std stays product-free per DESIGN open-decision #2):"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Part"), cell(text: "Layer"), cell(text: "Why")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "`EffectShape` (an effect: inputs/outputs/exit semantics)"), cell(text: "**std** (`std.effects`, exists)"), cell(text: "framework-level, no fleet knowledge")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "`HostEffect` coproduct, `NodeControlPlane`, `apply(target, effect, policy)`, `Receipt`"), cell(text: "**product**"), cell(text: "references `HostIdentity`/`BmcEndpoint`/`fleet_intent` (product); homing in std would drag product upward")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "concrete transports (Redfish / ssh / systemd), each citing its real spec, + the dispatch that selects them"), cell(text: "**extdeps**"), cell(text: "external authorities; dispatch is realization → peripheral")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "**Receipt:** generalize the converge lane's already-byte-locked receipt (#5725, fierce-carp) as the *single* `apply()` outcome — do **not** fork a second receipt grammar (§3 nickname trap). Confirm its located+typed core is **policy-agnostic** (carries `OneShotIdempotent` outcomes, not just drift-deltas); if it has converge-specific fields, generalize = common located/typed core + a policy-specific extension, never a parallel type. **Touch it WITH fierce-carp's lock, not around it.**"),
    h2(text: "1b. The effect-plan band — layer responsibilities + census decisions (operator, 2026-07-03)"),
    p(text: "Fork-census ruling: the orchestration layer is kept **only as the single effect-plan composition authority** — the composition algebra earns its keep (bounded composition over external effects is a real missing concept between pure computation and host-effect realization); the string/process leaves and duplicated neighbor vocabularies dissolve onto existing authorities. `v2.std.orchestration` renames to **`std.effect_plan`** at Phase B (\"orchestration\" reads shell/workflow-specific; the concept is broader)."),
    CodeBlock {
      code: "substrate           — control-flow behaviors + termination authority (Loop/measure; dag/std/termination.dag)\nstd.effect_plan     — bounded composition over external effects:\n                        seq · If\{predicate\} · While\{measure → DERIVED DescentEvidence\} · Retry\{ladder, on_exhausted\} · FailurePolicy\n                        leaves = Do\{effect\} — never a command string\nextdeps operations  — typed operation contracts (argv/process ops, git/tmux/claude, Redfish/REST); argv lives in transport rows\ngunbc.host_effect   — target + effect + idempotency/convergence evidence; apply(...) -> Reconciliation<Intent, Evidence>\nstd.upsert_decision — observe → classify → plan/remedy (temporal, os-install, leases, media all instantiate)\nstd.temporal_effect — durable attempt/receipt/lease/grant/await-approval spine\nmedia               — grammar rows; render/ingest at realization edges only"
    },
    p(text: "**Governance (RED rule):** a new type in this band must declare which layer responsibility it inhabits; overlap with an existing responsibility without an explicit de-fork plan fails review. Any unit introducing a new command/process/evidence/policy type must first prove why it is not one of the existing authorities."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Policy de-fork (the sharpest census finding):** `Policy.OneShotIdempotent` is the `idempotent: Bool` flag DESIGN records as already dissolved into `std.effects.EffectShape`, resurrected as a variant (`host_identity_converge` bridges the two per-site; ~30 other sites declare the literal bare). Fix: `HostEffectIntent` gains `IdempotencyEvidence` (the existing std authority); only a **derived** drive axis survives (`Drive = OneShot | ConvergeLoop`). Target the construction-first v2 `EffectShape` partition per the standing dag↔v2 de-fork direction (operator ruling 2026-07-03); no temporary third idempotency axis."),
      li(text: "**Evidence vs receipt — NOT a fork:** `apply()` returns `Reconciliation<HostEffectIntent, HostEffectEvidence>` — evidence is the domain payload (what was observed/applied), `Reconciliation` the generic carrier (how observed relates to desired). Keep the layering; do not collapse."),
      li(text: "**Decide-algebra consolidation:** `std.upsert_decision` owns observe→classify→plan. `std.temporal_effect` grounds `HeldLeaseObservedState`/`NextStepPlan` on it (5/5 verdict bijection; same-day concurrent mint #6171 vs #6187; `PlanAwaitApproval` is the honest temporal-only residue). `os_install_deduction`'s plan enum dissolves to `UpsertClassification<OsInstallRemedy, OsInstallRefusalReason>` — refusal reasons **typed** (operator ruling: strings are rendering, never authority); its preflight VERDICT vocabulary stays domain. `EffectStepReceipt.verdict_label`/`plan_label` are past their fired dissolve trigger (#6193 wired the folds) — dissolve now, typed against the unified plan algebra."),
      li(text: "**Retry vs temporal retry — DISTINCT, do not merge:** in-attempt mitigation ladder (detect → env delta → re-run, bounded by ladder) vs durable receipt-mediated convergence (pure fold over receipts/leases; iteration external; failure = refuse/await-approval, never automatic mitigation)."),
      li(text: "**Algebra grounding:** `Retry`/`While`/`If` are effect-plan *reflections* of substrate control-flow behaviors (body-lowering treats For/While/Retry/recursion as one `Loop` sugar). `While` carries a **measure** and DERIVES `DescentEvidence` from `dag/std/termination.dag` (ruled authority; the v2 cardinality copy repoints or is marked scaffold) — no measure ⇒ `While` unconstructible. `Retry.on_exhausted` is wired or narrowed before the slice-0 cutover. **Long-term dissolve trigger (NOT a near-term target):** effect-plan constructs lower to ordinary substrate graph fragments with `HostEffect` leaves + termination evidence; near-term the reified `EffectPlan` stays the §5 construction wall for the bounded fragment — effect plans carry domain facts (leaves, transport constraints, policy, receipt expectations) that must not casually collapse into generic computation."),
      li(text: "**Dead/duplicate vocab to clear:** `std.types.RetryCount` (zero consumers) — delete; `std.temporal_effect.TemporalEffectPolicy` (inert third effect-shape vocabulary; `CreateIfAbsent` name-collides `std.effects.CreateCause`) — dissolve or ground before any consumer; `gunbc.workflow.types` `RetryDue`/`Retryable` (zero importers) — converge onto the spine when wired; `HostExecArgv` (roadmap_dispatch_actuator) pays its 🟡 to extdeps git/tmux/claude service ops before a second consumer appears."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "2. Topology: star (push) → self-converge (pull)"),
    p(text: "The grid above admits the operator's minimal-dependency aim as a *cell*, not a rewrite:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Today / interim:** `transport=SshShell, policy=OneShotIdempotent` — a central actor reaches into hosts over SSH. Works, but it's the star: keys, central availability, passive hosts."),
      li(text: "**End-state:** `policy=ConvergeToFixpoint` running **on the host** — the host pulls its content-addressed `.dag` target-state and reconciles locally (systemd timer). No central SSH poker. The central job shrinks to (a) **emit** target state and (b) **kick BMC** for bare-metal bring-up."),
      li(text: "**Bootstrap chain (how a host gets to self-converge with minimal deps):** BMC out-of-band remote-boot (mechanism-agnostic — **VirtualMedia** or PXE, per what the node's BMC actually exposes) → Ubuntu autoinstall → the autoinstall seed plants the on-host self-converge agent (cloud-init/systemd unit) → host self-converges thereafter. The install/BMC lane (neat-boar) *is* the bootstrap; self-converge composes on top of it. This is the same Realization pattern as everywhere else: content-addressed pure-spec → host-effect. (Ground-truth: srv3's OpenBMC 2.07 exposes UpdateService + VirtualMedia paths but not PXE-over-Tailscale — PXE needs BIOS-net-stack + same-L2, can't cross the overlay — so **VirtualMedia is the Tailscale-agnostic primary** there. The interface is agnostic to which: both are `apply(BmcController, RedfishSystemAction)` arms; mechanism is a §3 realization detail, not an interface fact.)"),
    ]),
    h2(text: "3. Scoped, dependency-ordered plan"),
    p(text: "Each phase names its **displaced cost** (the pain removed) and its **dissolution/migration trigger**."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Phase A — mint the interface (model-before-implement). [LANDED #5756]** `gunbc.host_effect` (coproduct + `NodeControlPlane` + `Policy`) + `gunbc.host_effect_realize` (total dispatch fold, no `_ =>`; `ShellCommand@HostOs` realized over LocalShell grounded from observed exit; `RedfishAction@BmcController` fail-closed `Unimplemented` stub; incompatible cells = typed mismatch). Return reuses `std.realization_reconcile.Reconciliation` (no new receipt). `RedfishSystemAction` arm in `extdeps.bmc.types` (4 variants, co-owned neat-boar). Witness green-by-execution (real `sh` execs) + discriminating RED. *Scaffold: `ShellCommand \{ script: String \}` is a raw-string leaf — see Phase B for its dissolution.* *Displaced cost: the (1)/(2) fork — two paths for one concept.*"),
      li(text: "**Phase B — migrate `host_exec()` → `apply(target=HostOs, transport=SshShell, policy=OneShotIdempotent)`. [after neat-boar's srv3 `OsInstalled` milestone]** Sequenced *after* the live install reaches `OsInstalled` so B migrates a **proven-working** seam, not a racing install (neat-boar's ask). The seam is the single migration point; every `host_exec` call moves in one mechanical pass. Install behavior unchanged, now on the interface. **Dissolution trigger (the Phase-A `ShellCommand\{script:String\}` scaffold):** `host_exec` carries script *strings*, so B migrates them 1:1 onto `ShellCommand\{script\}` — then `ShellCommand`'s payload dissolves *jointly with* those strings onto modeled **effect-plan intent** (a `v2.std.orchestration` `Pipeline` — the [shell-emission-model](shell-emission-model.md) supersession of this item's original `program.dag` pointer), symmetric to `RedfishAction` being typed. **Invocation-vs-script distinction (census 2026-07-03):** most `host_exec`/`ShellCommand` strings are process *invocations* (typed argv → exit/stdout), not bash-the-language — those leaves land as typed extdeps operations (the service-op transport-argv mechanism; **reuse or EXTEND that authority — no new `std.ProcessInvocation`**), with `Pipeline` composing them; bash spelling appears only at pre-runtime realization edges per the bash-minimization rule. Forcing the payload change in A would couple two changes; deferring keeps B a clean 1:1 migration. *Displaced cost: a bespoke ssh seam that can't express non-ssh effects (e.g. BMC); + the raw-shell-string anemic leaf.*"),
      li(text: "**Phase C — BMC effects as the `RedfishAction` arm over `RedfishRest`.** `apply(target=BmcController, effect=BootSourceOverride\{Pxe,Once\})` → `Reset\{ForceRestart\}`, outcome observed via async poll. This is the transport that **proves the interface isn't ssh-with-extra-steps** — it forces target-duality, structured (non-string) effects, and async receipts into the shape; an ssh-only executor literally *can't* express it. *Displaced cost: BMC ops stranded outside the model — and the only path to pre-OS phases.*"),
      li(text: "**Phase D — converge lane → `EmitArtifactThenThinRun` handler; begin ctrl deletion.** `host_converge`/`fleet_converge_emit` become one transport handler bound to the same shape; **delete `runner_host_reconcile.mjs`'s hash/fan-out** (first net ctrl deletion) and `defaultContainerResourceCaps` heuristic (cap inherited from the emitted slice). *`EmitArtifactThenThinRun` is currently prose-only — this phase MODELS the transport arm; the shell-emission converge thin-run slice consumes it. Guardrail: the binary interprets a typed plan and emits typed receipts — an opaque imperative driver is no progress over an opaque script.* *Displaced cost: ctrl JS owning host-apply; metric = ctrl LOC deleted.*"),
      li(text: "**Phase E — self-converge policy (the minimal-topology payoff).** `policy=ConvergeToFixpoint` realized **on-host** (pull target-state + systemd-timer reconcile); autoinstall seed plants the agent. Retire the central SSH-star for steady-state management; central role shrinks to emit + BMC-kick. *Displaced cost: the star topology — keys, central availability, passive hosts.*"),
      li(text: "**Phase F — decom as the reverse fold (stubs now).** Extend the lifecycle `FactoryDefault→CredsRotated→OsInstalled→FabricJoined→Drained→Decommissioned` against `fleet_intent` (§4 one procedure, both directions). Land the decom operations (`drain → deregister-from-offers → revoke-creds → secure-erase-drives → BMC power-off/factory-reset`) as **fail-closed stubs** — typed `Unimplemented`/refuse, **never a plausible no-op** (a silent drive-wipe/power-off \"success\" is the exact §5 trap). Declares the shape, does nothing, can't be mistaken for working. *Implementation trigger: a real decom use case.*"),
    ]),
    h2(text: "4. Coherence + test (the deliverable's proof)"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "One interface, one fleet authority (`fleet_intent`), one receipt grammar — the §3 single-authority test: net concepts must not grow by re-invention."),
      li(text: "**End-to-end lifecycle witness** green by execution over the interface (install slice already proven on the seam; re-prove on `apply()` post-migration), with discriminating fail-closed controls (drop an input → typed refusal; decom stub → typed `Unimplemented`, not success)."),
      li(text: "ctrl-LOC-deleted tracked per phase (D/E) as the honest progress metric."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "Ownership"),
    p(text: "The `HostEffect` coproduct must not fork — arms co-design, the shape mints as one unit:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**smart-newt-512** — the `ShellCommand` arm + `HostOs` control-plane + central `apply()`/dispatch + Receipt generalization (with fierce-carp); converge-lane migration + ctrl-exodus (Phase A/D), management/caps side."),
      li(text: "**neat-boar-71** — the `RedfishAction` arm + `BmcController` control-plane + bmc extdeps (has the live srv3 evidence + the Redfish spec); install/BMC bootstrap + transports (Phase B/C/E bootstrap). Continues srv3 install on `host_exec()` through `OsInstalled`, then migrates."),
      li(text: "**Co-owned, lands together in Phase A:** the `HostEffect` coproduct, `NodeControlPlane`, and the `apply()` signature — so neither arm is minted alone."),
      li(text: "Decom (Phase F) co-owned; fail-closed stubs land with the interface."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data host_effect_orchestration_plan: Plan = Plan {
  slug: "host-effect-orchestration",
  title: "Host-effect orchestration — interface + shell→.dag migration plan",
  body: host_effect_orchestration_body(),
  dissolution: HasTrigger {
    text: "Delete this doc when the `apply(target, effect, policy) -> Receipt` interface is minted in product (the `HostEffect` coproduct + `NodeControlPlane` co-owned as one unit), every `host_exec()` call is migrated onto it, the BMC `RedfishAction` arm over `RedfishRest` and the converge-lane `EmitArtifactThenThinRun` handler have landed, ctrl host-apply LOC (the `runner_host_reconcile.mjs` hash/fan-out + `defaultContainerResourceCaps`) is deleted, and the on-host self-converge policy + the decom reverse-fold are realized (or their fail-closed `Unimplemented` stubs are witnessed) — at which point the lifecycle is one tested interface and this design note is redundant."
  }
}
